e f-strings have double quotes that are part of the Python source. I'll do the replacement.\n\nLet me copy the string and replace:\n\nOriginal (with \\n but no escaped quotes):\ndef solve(case):\n    from fractions import Fraction\n    segments = case['segments']\n    budget = case['budget']\n    # Validate\n    if not segments:\n        raise ValueError(\"No segments\")\n    total_min = 0\n    total_cap = 0\n    for seg in segments:\n        total_min += seg['minimum']\n        total_cap += seg['capacity']\n    if budget < total_min:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Budget {budget} less than total minimum {total_min}\")\n    if budget > total_cap:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Budget {budget} exceeds total capacity {total_cap}\")\n    # Initialize allocations\n    alloc = {}\n    for seg in segments:\n        alloc[seg['name']] = seg['minimum']\n    remaining = budget - total_min\n    # While budget remains\n    while remaining > 0:\n        best_idx = None\n        best_frac = None\n        for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\n            name = seg['name']\n            if alloc[name] >= seg['capacity']:\n                continue\n            # Compute ratio = importance / (allocated + 1)\n            frac = Fraction(seg['importance'], alloc[name] + 1)\n            if best_frac is None or frac > best_frac or (frac == best_frac and i < best_idx):\n                best_frac = frac\n                best_idx = i\n        if best_idx is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"No available slot\")\n        seg = segments[best_idx]\n        alloc[seg['name']] += 1\n        remaining -= 1\n    # Build name_mapping\n    name_mapping = [seg['name'] for seg in segments]\n    total = sum(alloc.values())\n    return {\n        \"allocations\": alloc,\n        \"name_mapping\": name_mapping,\n        \"total\": total\n    }\n\nNow replace each \" with \\\". I'll go line by line and produce the escaped version. I'll write it as a continuous string.\n\nLine1: def solve(case):\\n\nLine2: 